  "season": 2,
  "episode": 22,
  "showTitle": "The Hard Saying",
  "title": "St. Joseph",
  "dates": "Monday, March 15 – Sunday, March 21, 2010",
  "logline": "A second Wednesday with a very long book, a table built for a saint by someone who said to leave it with her, and a call from Ohio on a Friday in Lent; on Sunday the House votes, and nobody in the Fishbowl is happy about it.",
  "previously": [
    {
      "text": "In Morro 1100, Skye: “From the beginning. In order. One section at a time.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "At Low Tide, Skye: “Fine,” … “Chapter One, Roman numeral one, to you. Don’t get used to it.” … “‘Ways of Coming to Know God.’ Next Wednesday. Bring proofs.”",
      "if": "duel.cat1.heart<=1 && duel.cat1.rigor>=2"
    },
    {
      "text": "At Low Tide, Skye: “Draw,” … “I hate draws.” … “‘Ways of Coming to Know God.’ Next Wednesday. Bring proofs.”",
      "if": "duel.cat1.heart>=2"
    },
    {
      "text": "At Low Tide, Skye: “Mine,” … “Write it down.” … “‘Ways of Coming to Know God.’ Next Wednesday. Bring proofs.”",
      "if": "duel.cat1.heart<=1 && duel.cat1.rigor<=1"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the hall outside 217, Lena: “Did she keep her hands to herself?” — You: “Yes.” — Lena: “Then it’s Wednesday.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the east stairwell, Lena: “Nobody has ever thought this hard about me for two dollars and fifty cents.” — You: “It wasn’t hard.” — Lena: “That’s what I mean.”",
      "if": "s2e21_hour==\"sincerity\""
    },
    {
      "text": "In the east stairwell, Lena: “Nobody has ever thought this hard about me for two dollars and fifty cents.” — You: “I’ve been thinking about the socks since Thursday.”",
      "if": "s2e21_hour==\"candor\""
    },
    {
      "text": "In the east stairwell, Lena: “Nobody has ever thought this hard about me for two dollars and fifty cents.” — You: “Five. There were two games.” — Lena: “*Five*,” … “Lord have mercy.”",
      "if": "s2e21_hour==\"wit\""
    },
    {
      "text": "In the east stairwell, Lena: “Nobody has ever thought this hard about me for two dollars and fifty cents.”",
      "if": "s2e21_hour!=\"sincerity\" && s2e21_hour!=\"candor\" && s2e21_hour!=\"wit\""
    },
    {
      "text": "Under the olive tree, Lena: “I *know* what Friday is,” … “Did you think I’d forget?” … “Leave it with me.”",
      "if": "s2e17_wed==\"house\""
    },
    {
      "text": "Under the olive tree, Lena: “You were born on St. Joseph’s Day,” … “and you didn’t *tell* me?” … “Leave it with me.”",
      "if": "s2e17_wed!=\"house\""
    },
    {
      "text": "You: “We haven’t done anything for it since Danny went away.”",
      "if": "s2e21_joseph==\"candor\""
    }
  ],
